{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793699911,"nonce":"6lWdbgMjFWl48Xho08NYiA9vuZ4=","message":"Fixed in the flow move (280f391): render_flow takes the element's effective clip (primary intersected with scroll clip, as text and SVG use) and scissors to bounds ∩ target ∩ clip. The viewport is now the full element bounds, so a flow partly off the target or clipped keeps its uv mapping; it was clamped and the shader squeezed into the visible part (SDF rings drew as ellipses). Overlay clips arrive through the same current_clip. Only rect clips are honoured: a rounded or path clip on an ancestor does not round the flow, which uses its own corner_radius uniform. Regression test: canvas_flow_tests::a_canvas_flow_stops_at_its_ancestors_clip_and_keeps_its_uv (ignored, needs GPU).","files":null}]}